          "line": 24,
          "text": "| X2 | **Long-lived third-party credentials sit in every session's env, and two are unused.** `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` is an AKIA (IAM-user, long-lived) key with no session token, used by one perf tool. `GROK_API_KEY` (xai-) is referenced only by an archived note. `FLEET_A_OAUTH_TOKEN` (sk-ant-oat) is still referenced by no code. | env shape check (prefix and length only); `git grep`: AWS \u2192 tools/perf/devicefarm-iphone.mjs + 1 doc, GROK \u2192 docs/archive/notes/GROK-API-2026-10-22.md only, FLEET_A \u2192 audit notes only; AWS-DEVICE-FARM-IPHONE-2026-10-23.md:11-13 (IAM user apex-devicefarm-agent) | Every worker that reads untrusted text holds an AWS key, an xAI key and another account's OAuth token (~60 sessions/day). Leak cost: AWS bill or Device Farm abuse, Grok spend | Delete GROK_API_KEY and FLEET_A_OAUTH_TOKEN from env \"I\". Move the AWS pair to a perf-only env and confirm the IAM policy is `devicefarm:*` only | high | STILL OPEN (pass3 E3) + NEW (AWS, GROK) |"
